  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 229 PM MDT Fri Sep 18 2026\nUpdated at 205 AM.\n\nMonday through the end of the week is looking fairly consistent\nforecast wise. High temperatures are forecast in the 60s to 70s\nwith afternoon PoPs around 30-50% due to embedded shortwave and\njet support. Starting Monday, we transition to more of a zonal \nupper- level pattern with a jet streak overhead. Early \nWednesday, we are forecast to transition to a weak ridging \npattern with a jet streak remaining overhead. The jet streak \noverhead the CWA will cause windy conditions Tuesday afternoon \nthrough Wednesday with gusts from 30-40 mph possible for the \nwestern CWA. Increased jet support is expected to remain over \nthe area through at least Thursday, but models diverge on when \nthe jet streak will move on. This will ultimately affect \nprecipitation chances for the CWA.",
